  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table><thead><tr><th><div>TLC Level</div></th><th><div>Interpretation</div></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><div>Below Normal Range</div></td><td><div>Reduced TLC levels (leukopenia) may indicate bone marrow suppression, viral infections, autoimmune diseases, certain medications, or nutritional deficiencies. Further evaluation is needed to determine the underlying cause.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Normal Range</div></td><td><div>TLC levels within the normal range indicate a healthy leukocyte count.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Above Normal Range</div></td><td><div>Elevated TLC levels (leukocytosis) may suggest bacterial infections, inflammation, tissue damage, stress, certain medications, leukemia, or other hematological disorders. Further evaluation is necessary to identify the underlying cause.</div></td></tr></tbody></table>",
